    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d425c05b_5b647893",
        "filename": "floss/hcidoc/src/parser.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 121,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836438
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-09T19:24:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Because you need the given timestamp to convert. You can have a constant function but not a constant value to do the translation.\n```\nTS_IN_MS \u003d ((given_ts - Y2K_EPOCH_CONST) / 1000) + Y2K_OFFSET_MS \n```",
      "parentUuid": "cf73384f_241b994f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 121,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 121,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "d5bfb1dc19774633a8f4dca6c68de70f416574da",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5c937f94_b96e11fa",
        "filename": "floss/hcidoc/src/parser.rs",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 121,
      "author": {
        "id": 1960535
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-10T03:57:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "```\nTS_IN_MS \u003d ((given_ts - Y2K_EPOCH_CONST) / 1000) + Y2K_OFFSET_MS \n         \u003d (given_ts/1000) - (Y2K_EPOCH_CONST/1000) + Y2K_OFFSET_MS\n```\n\nNow we can define the single constant YEAR_0_TO_1970 as follows\n```\nYEAR_0_TO_1970 \u003d Y2K_OFFSET_MS - (Y2K_EPOCH_CONST/1000)\n```\n\nEffectively having only one constant instead of two, we can formulate\n```\nTS_IN_MS \u003d given_ts/1000 + YEAR_0_TO_1970\n```",
      "parentUuid": "d425c05b_5b647893",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 121,
        "startChar": 6,
        "endLine": 121,
        "endChar": 31
      },
